<decompilertest>
<binaryimage arch="x86:LE:64:default:gcc">
<!--
    Option flowmode (GH-780): ARM code that control flow proves the mode of is
    painted with that mode where the Listing walk's own blx writes left the
    other one.

    The XML wrapper only provides the harness architecture. The script loads
    two stripped fixtures (one generator beside them) with the Listing walk on,
    as every CLI surface runs it on ARM. In each, an A32 entry at 0x2000000
    calls a Thumb helper at 0x2000040 (`movs r0,#7; bx lr`) with `blx` and an
    A32 helper at 0x2000080 (`add r0,r0,#1; bx lr`) with `bl`. No symbol or
    mapping symbol names either mode. Decoding the `blx` writes Thumb into the
    context database from 0x2000040 to the end of the address space, so the
    walk leaves the A32 helper in Thumb, and the decompiler prints
    `halt_missing()` for it (a Thumb decode starting at 0x2000082).

    Pass 1, `arm_interwork_bl_first_le32` (the `bl` comes first), the default
    (off): the A32 helper prints `halt_missing()`.

    Pass 2, the same image, option on: the entry's even address proves A32
    and its first call, the `bl`, proves the A32 helper, which makes no call
    and is painted A32. It returns `a0 + 1`.

    Pass 3, `arm_interwork_le32` (the `blx` comes first, the issue's layout),
    option on: the `bl` comes after a call, and nothing proves that call
    returns at its site, so nothing is painted and the helper still prints
    `halt_missing()`.

    Pass 4, the same image, option aftercall: the Thumb helper is proven to
    return, so the `bl` after the `blx` is proven too. The A32 helper returns
    `a0 + 1`, the Thumb helper returns 7, and the entry passes the Thumb
    result to the A32 helper.
-->
<bytechunk space="ram" offset="0x100000" readonly="true">
c3
</bytechunk>
<symbol space="ram" offset="0x100000" name="harness_stub"/>
</binaryimage>
<script>
  <com>clear architecture</com>
  <com>load file decompiler/crates/kuna-analysis/tests/fixtures/arm_interwork_bl_first_le32</com>
  <com>option listing on</com>
  <com>read symbols</com>
  <com>load addr 0x2000080</com>
  <com>decompile</com>
  <com>print C</com>
  <com>clear architecture</com>
  <com>load file decompiler/crates/kuna-analysis/tests/fixtures/arm_interwork_bl_first_le32</com>
  <com>option listing on</com>
  <com>option flowmode on</com>
  <com>read symbols</com>
  <com>load addr 0x2000080</com>
  <com>decompile</com>
  <com>print C</com>
  <com>clear architecture</com>
  <com>load file decompiler/crates/kuna-analysis/tests/fixtures/arm_interwork_le32</com>
  <com>option listing on</com>
  <com>option flowmode on</com>
  <com>read symbols</com>
  <com>load addr 0x2000080</com>
  <com>decompile</com>
  <com>print C</com>
  <com>clear architecture</com>
  <com>load file decompiler/crates/kuna-analysis/tests/fixtures/arm_interwork_le32</com>
  <com>option listing on</com>
  <com>option flowmode aftercall</com>
  <com>read symbols</com>
  <com>load addr 0x2000080</com>
  <com>decompile</com>
  <com>print C</com>
  <com>load addr 0x2000040</com>
  <com>decompile</com>
  <com>print C</com>
  <com>load addr 0x2000000</com>
  <com>decompile</com>
  <com>print C</com>
  <com>quit</com>
</script>
<stringmatch name="FLOWMODE #1: off (the default), and on after an unproven call, the A32 helper decodes as Thumb" min="2" max="2">halt_missing</stringmatch>
<stringmatch name="FLOWMODE #2: on, the first bl target keeps A32; aftercall, the bl after the blx does" min="2" max="2">return a0 \+ 1;</stringmatch>
<stringmatch name="FLOWMODE #3: aftercall, the blx target decodes as Thumb and returns 7" min="1" max="1">return 7;</stringmatch>
<stringmatch name="FLOWMODE #4: aftercall, the entry passes the Thumb result to the A32 helper" min="1" max="1">sub_2000080\(sub_2000040\(\)\)</stringmatch>
</decompilertest>
